1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,606
Your body temperature is not fixed.

2
00:00:02,606 --> 00:00:07,118
It is lowest around four in the morning,
and highest in the late afternoon.

3
00:00:07,518 --> 00:00:11,032
Across a day it shifts by
about half a degree Celsius.

4
00:00:11,032 --> 00:00:13,427
Every hour gives exactly one reading.

5
00:00:13,877 --> 00:00:16,461
Diya tracked this for her biology notes.

6
00:00:16,811 --> 00:00:21,210
One hour in, one number out, and the
number can be thirty six point eight.

7
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:23,048
What kind of function is that?

8
00:00:23,548 --> 00:00:25,973
It has a name: a real valued function.

9
00:00:25,973 --> 00:00:28,904
Let us see why, and what
makes a real function.

10
00:00:29,554 --> 00:00:33,741
Recall: a function sends each
input to exactly one output.

11
00:00:34,091 --> 00:00:38,627
If every output is a real number,
the function is called real valued.

12
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:41,044
Its range is R, or a part of R.

13
00:00:41,444 --> 00:00:46,406
If its inputs are real numbers too,
so its domain is also R or a part of

14
00:00:46,406 --> 00:00:48,871
R, it is called a real function.

15
00:00:49,521 --> 00:00:51,263
Watch Diya's function run.

16
00:00:51,263 --> 00:00:53,225
The input is the hour, h.

17
00:00:53,225 --> 00:00:55,587
The output is the temperature, T.

18
00:00:55,987 --> 00:00:58,991
The hour counts up, and
the curve draws itself.

19
00:00:58,991 --> 00:01:01,328
One dot for each moment, never two.

20
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,923
At four in the morning, the
curve hits its lowest point.

21
00:01:04,923 --> 00:01:06,985
In the late afternoon, its highest.

22
00:01:07,385 --> 00:01:09,817
Inputs are real numbers of hours.

23
00:01:09,817 --> 00:01:12,409
Outputs are real numbers of degrees.

24
00:01:12,409 --> 00:01:14,518
So this is a real function.

25
00:01:15,168 --> 00:01:16,373
Side by side.

26
00:01:16,373 --> 00:01:19,629
Diya's function takes
hours and gives degrees.

27
00:01:19,629 --> 00:01:21,057
Both are numbers.

28
00:01:21,057 --> 00:01:22,428
A real function.

29
00:01:22,828 --> 00:01:24,312
Now a different rule.

30
00:01:24,312 --> 00:01:27,377
Each student goes to their
height in centimetres.

31
00:01:27,377 --> 00:01:30,749
The outputs are real numbers,
so it is real valued.

32
00:01:30,749 --> 00:01:33,467
But the inputs are students, not numbers.

33
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:36,736
So, is the height rule a real function?

34
00:01:36,736 --> 00:01:37,965
Pause and decide.

35
00:01:41,165 --> 00:01:42,065
No!

36
00:01:41,614 --> 00:01:45,343
Its range is real, but its
domain is a set of students.

37
00:01:45,343 --> 00:01:48,310
It is real valued, but
not a real function.

38
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,213
Remember this.

39
00:01:50,213 --> 00:01:52,674
Real valued means real outputs.

40
00:01:52,674 --> 00:01:56,399
Real function means real
inputs and real outputs.

41
00:01:57,099 --> 00:02:02,081
A real function from your NCERT book:
t of C equals nine C over five, plus

42
00:02:02,081 --> 00:02:03,014
thirty two.

43
00:02:03,014 --> 00:02:05,246
It turns Celsius into Fahrenheit.

44
00:02:05,646 --> 00:02:06,567
Step one.

45
00:02:06,567 --> 00:02:07,723
Put in zero.

46
00:02:07,723 --> 00:02:10,383
Nine times zero over five is zero.

47
00:02:10,383 --> 00:02:11,708
Add thirty two.

48
00:02:11,708 --> 00:02:14,582
Water freezes at thirty two Fahrenheit.

49
00:02:15,332 --> 00:02:16,232
Step two.

50
00:02:16,164 --> 00:02:19,441
Put in thirty seven, a
typical body temperature.

51
00:02:19,441 --> 00:02:22,780
That gives sixty six point
six, plus thirty two.

52
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,444
Ninety eight point six.

53
00:02:25,194 --> 00:02:26,094
Step three.

54
00:02:26,065 --> 00:02:27,429
Put in one hundred.

55
00:02:27,429 --> 00:02:30,005
That gives one eighty, plus thirty two.

56
00:02:30,005 --> 00:02:32,723
Two hundred and twelve, where water boils.

57
00:02:33,473 --> 00:02:34,835
Watch C count up.

58
00:02:34,835 --> 00:02:38,321
Each Celsius value gives
exactly one Fahrenheit value.

59
00:02:38,321 --> 00:02:40,994
The points line up in a straight line.

60
00:02:41,644 --> 00:02:44,132
Often a question gives only the rule.

61
00:02:44,132 --> 00:02:48,524
Then the domain is every real number
x for which the rule gives a real

62
00:02:48,524 --> 00:02:49,424
number.

63
00:02:49,575 --> 00:02:52,665
Take f of x equals one over x minus two.

64
00:02:52,665 --> 00:02:54,898
Scan x along the number line.

65
00:02:55,298 --> 00:02:57,278
Every x works, except two.

66
00:02:57,278 --> 00:03:01,829
At two, the bottom becomes zero,
and we can never divide by zero.

67
00:03:01,829 --> 00:03:03,982
So the domain is R minus two.

68
00:03:04,382 --> 00:03:07,121
Now take the square root of x minus one.

69
00:03:07,121 --> 00:03:10,203
The number under the root
must not be negative.

70
00:03:10,203 --> 00:03:12,088
So x must be one or more.

71
00:03:12,738 --> 00:03:13,655
Quick one.

72
00:03:13,655 --> 00:03:17,483
Is x equal to one in the
domain of root x minus one?

73
00:03:17,483 --> 00:03:18,780
Pause and think.

74
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:22,880
Yes!

75
00:03:22,498 --> 00:03:26,799
The root of one minus one is
the root of zero, which is zero.

76
00:03:26,799 --> 00:03:28,635
So one is in the domain.

77
00:03:29,285 --> 00:03:31,020
Now, one worked example.

78
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:36,482
Find the domain of f of x equals x
squared plus two x plus one, over x

79
00:03:36,482 --> 00:03:39,011
squared minus eight x plus twelve.

80
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:40,411
Step one.

81
00:03:40,344 --> 00:03:42,448
The top is fine for every x.

82
00:03:42,448 --> 00:03:44,796
Only the bottom can cause trouble.

83
00:03:45,546 --> 00:03:46,446
Step two.

84
00:03:46,436 --> 00:03:47,878
Factor the bottom.

85
00:03:47,878 --> 00:03:53,030
x squared minus eight x plus twelve
is x minus two, times x minus six.

86
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,721
Step three.

87
00:03:54,721 --> 00:03:57,639
The bottom is zero when x is two or six.

88
00:03:58,389 --> 00:03:59,303
Step four.

89
00:03:59,303 --> 00:04:01,456
Remove only those two numbers.

90
00:04:01,456 --> 00:04:04,439
The domain is R minus the set two, six.

91
00:04:05,189 --> 00:04:07,275
Notice: we never needed the top.

92
00:04:07,275 --> 00:04:09,352
With fractions, watch the bottom.

93
00:04:10,002 --> 00:04:11,467
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:04:11,817 --> 00:04:15,847
Find the domain of x squared
minus four, over x minus two.

95
00:04:15,847 --> 00:04:17,715
Many students cancel first.

96
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:21,501
They get x plus two, and
say the domain is all of R.

97
00:04:21,901 --> 00:04:25,174
But the domain belongs to
the rule as it is given.

98
00:04:25,174 --> 00:04:29,388
At x equals two the bottom is
zero, so two is still not allowed.

99
00:04:29,388 --> 00:04:31,222
The domain is R minus two.

100
00:04:31,872 --> 00:04:33,350
Where is this asked?

101
00:04:33,350 --> 00:04:37,954
In JEE Main, as find the domain of
a function with fractions, roots and

102
00:04:37,954 --> 00:04:38,854
logs.

103
00:04:38,509 --> 00:04:42,756
In PUC boards, as find the domain
and range of a real function.

104
00:04:43,356 --> 00:04:44,570
Exam level now.

105
00:04:44,570 --> 00:04:48,171
How many integers are in
the domain of this function?

106
00:04:48,171 --> 00:04:49,437
Pause and solve.

107
00:04:54,837 --> 00:04:56,010
The answer is B.

108
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:56,910
Five.

109
00:04:57,020 --> 00:05:00,961
Under the root, nine minus x
squared must be zero or more.

110
00:05:00,961 --> 00:05:03,472
So x runs from minus three to three.

111
00:05:03,972 --> 00:05:07,607
The bottom, x squared minus
one, must not be zero.

112
00:05:07,607 --> 00:05:09,992
So x cannot be one or minus one.

113
00:05:10,492 --> 00:05:13,842
The integers from minus three
to three are seven numbers.

114
00:05:14,342 --> 00:05:16,198
Remove minus one and one.

115
00:05:16,198 --> 00:05:17,889
Five integers are left.

116
00:05:18,489 --> 00:05:19,950
Here is your recap.

117
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,451
Screenshot this card.

118
00:05:24,651 --> 00:05:27,488
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

119
00:05:27,888 --> 00:05:28,788
One.

120
00:05:28,386 --> 00:05:33,004
What is the difference between a real
valued function and a real function?

121
00:05:33,904 --> 00:05:34,804
Two.

122
00:05:34,469 --> 00:05:39,684
Find t of minus forty, for t of C
equals nine C over five, plus thirty

123
00:05:39,684 --> 00:05:40,584
two.

124
00:05:41,148 --> 00:05:42,048
Three.

125
00:05:41,777 --> 00:05:45,179
Find the domain of one
over x squared minus nine.

126
00:05:46,279 --> 00:05:51,236
Next time: a fixed bus fare, a
mirror, and the area of a square plot.

127
00:05:51,236 --> 00:05:53,563
Three rules, three famous graphs.

128
00:05:53,563 --> 00:05:56,446
Constant, identity and
polynomial functions.
